# Thesis study assets are addressed by content hash: the oracle refuses to run
# unless the bytes on disk match the pin recorded in `assets-manifest.json` and
# each `oracle.json`. With `core.autocrlf=true` a fresh clone rewrites their line
# endings, every pin goes stale and the frozen instrument becomes unrunnable on
# any machine but the one that produced it. Never convert them.
/docs/tesis/evidence/warehouse/** -text
/docs/tesis/evidence/scripts/** -text

# Imported by `oracle-core.mjs` to spawn pnpm, so it is part of the pinned
# instrument surface for the same reason.
/scripts/manyhands-dev-command.mjs -text

# Stage 0 hashes raw receipts byte-for-byte. Keep their committed bytes stable
# across checkout-level line-ending settings.
/docs/audits/stage-0/logs/** -text -diff
